      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Metaphase:

    In metaphase, the spindle has captured all the chromosomes
    and lined them up at the middle of the cell, ready to divide. All the chromosomes
    align at the metaphase plate (not a physical structure, just a term for the plane
    where the chromosomes line up). Before proceeding to anaphase, the cell will
    check to make sure that all the chromosomes are at the metaphase plate.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
